e the index.json  \n✅ **Flexible** - Can still use remote URLs when needed\n\n### Test Results\n\n- ✅ TypeScript compilation: **PASSED**\n- ✅ Build: **SUCCEEDED**\n- ✅ Tests: **48/50 passing** (2 pre-existing failures unrelated to this feature)\n- ✅ New integration tests: **6/6 passing**\n\n### Important Notes\n\n**For Server-Only Mode (Browser Extraction):**\nEven if you use `--index-file`, you still need `--storybook-url` for server-only mode because the browser needs to navigate to the actual Storybook pages. The index file is only used for component discovery.\n\n```bash\n# This will fail (server-only mode requires storybookUrl for browser)\nstorybook-to-skill-md generate \\\n  --index-file ./storybook-static/index.json \\\n  --server-only\n\n# This works (has both index file AND url for browser navigation)\nstorybook-to-skill-md generate \\\n  --index-file ./storybook-static/index.json \\\n  --storybook-url https://your-storybook.com \\\n  --server-only\n```\n\n**For Local File Mode (Recommended):**\nYou can use ONLY `--index-file` when you have source files locally:\n```bash\n# This works! Fully offline with no Storybook server needed\nstorybook-to-skill-md generate \\\n  --index-file ./storybook-static/index.json \\\n  --source-dir ./src/components \\\n  --output-dir ./skills\n```\n\nThe feature is complete and ready to use! 🎉",
