            "content": "# Storybook to SKILL.md Documentation\n\nWelcome to the comprehensive documentation for `storybook-to-skill-md` - a CLI tool that generates [SKILL.md](https://agentskills.io) files from your Storybook components for AI agents.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Getting Started](./getting-started.md) - Quick installation and first run\n- [Configuration](./configuration.md) - Complete configuration reference\n- [CLI Reference](./cli-reference.md) - All CLI options and flags\n- [Use Cases](./use-cases.md) - Real-world examples and recipes\n- [How It Works](./how-it-works.md) - Architecture and internals\n- [LLM Providers](./providers.md) - OpenAI, Anthropic, Google setup\n- [GitHub Action](./github-action.md) - CI/CD integration guide\n- [Troubleshooting](./troubleshooting.md) - Common issues and solutions\n\n## Quick Links\n\n- [GitHub Repository](https://github.com/sergiocarracedo/storybook-to-skill-md)\n- [npm Package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/storybook-to-skill-md)\n- [GitHub Action](https://github.com/sergiocarracedo/storybook-to-skill-md-action)\n- [Report Issues](https://github.com/sergiocarracedo/storybook-to-skill-md/issues)\n\n## What is SKILL.md?\n\nSKILL.md files are specially formatted markdown files that provide AI agents with structured knowledge about your components. They follow the [agentskills.io](https://agentskills.io) specification and include:\n\n- Component description and purpose\n- Props/API documentation\n- Usage examples from Storybook stories\n- Implementation guidelines\n- Common patterns and variations\n\n## Why Use This Tool?\n\n- **Automated Documentation** - Generate component docs automatically from Storybook\n- **AI-Friendly Format** - Optimized for AI agent consumption\n- **Always Up-to-Date** - Regenerate on every change using caching\n- **Multiple Modes** - Work with deployed Storybook or local builds\n- **LLM-Powered** - Uses GPT-4, Claude, or Gemini to generate high-quality docs\n- **CI/CD Ready** - GitHub Action for automated generation\n\n## Support\n\nIf you need help:\n\n1. Check the [Troubleshooting](./troubleshooting.md) guide\n2. Search [existing issues](https://github.com/sergiocarracedo/storybook-to-skill-md/issues)\n3. Create a [new issue](https://github.com/sergiocarracedo/storybook-to-skill-md/issues/new)\n\n## Contributing\n\nContributions are welcome! Please see our [Contributing Guide](../CONTRIBUTING.md) (coming soon).\n\n## License\n\nMIT © [Sergio Carracedo](https://github.com/sergiocarracedo)\n",
